### Note on the emoji symbol artwork

The 57 card symbols and the 3 HUD icons come from Google's Noto Color Emoji.
Per the upstream README, "Tools and most image resources are under the Apache
license, version 2.0" (https://github.com/googlefonts/noto-emoji).

The provenance is established by the original Unity project, which stored these
files under `Assets/Resources/NotoEmoji/` and added them in a commit titled
"Added emoji fonts". The files are not byte-identical to the upstream 128px
PNGs: 14 of the 57 are 136×128 indexed-color PNGs and one carries an
`Adobe ImageReady` text chunk, so they were re-saved after download. A
pixel-level comparison against the upstream release has not been performed.

### Note on the sound effects

The two sound effects were added to the original Unity project in 2020 under the
filenames `wood_plank_flicks.wav` and `instrument_strum.wav`. Neither that
repository nor this one records where they came from, and no attribution or
license text accompanied them. They ship in the App Store and Google Play
releases that have been public since 2020. Treat the license column above as
unverified rather than as a claim of permission, and replace these files with
assets of known provenance if the origin cannot be established.
